SK8V is an unofficial fan project, unaffiliated with EA, Rockstar Games or
Take-Two Interactive. It contains no GTA V or Skate 3 code or data; players
convert their own copies. ScriptHookV is not included: it is fetched from
Alexander Blade's official distribution (dev-c.com) and the ASI links against
its SDK import library.

Real-time collision detection: credit to Sol4ra. The live GTA collision reader
(host/src/physics_level.*, rust/skatev-runtime/src/live.rs) is adapted for
Legacy from Sol4ra's LS-Skate-LiveCollision (GTA V Enhanced), shared with
SK8V by its author.

This product builds on the following third-party work.

Skate engine (Apache-2.0)
  2010 Rust Rewrite Mashup, by chasmlol, a fork of IW4L by vladtrc.
  https://github.com/chasmlol/2010-rust-rewrite-mashup
  Copyright 2026 vladtrc; Skate engine by chasmlol.
  Fetched at the commit pinned in upstreams.lock.json; patches/skate/ holds
  SK8V's modifications to it. Its Skate 3 engine crates (skate-core,
  skate-data, skate-host, skate-net) are compiled into SkateVRuntime.dll.

Skate 3 HUD and asset pipeline (Apache-2.0 by grant)
  skate-3-rust-engine HUD modules (apt_vm, apt_display, apt_movie, apt_text,
  apt_scene, hud_runtime) and asset-pipeline exports, by chasmlol, used under
  chasmlol's Apache-2.0 grant of 2026-10-07 at commit cb796893.
  https://github.com/SK8-ENGINE/skate-3-rust-engine
  rust/skate-hud compiles the HUD modules in place from the fetched upstream
  (no donor source is copied into this repository); tools/convert-skate-data.py
  runs the exports during setup. Later revisions of that repository are
  GPL-3.0 and are used as reference only.

EA-XMA audio decoder (LGPL-2.1-or-later)
  rust/skate-xma is a port of FFmpeg 4.4's xmaframes / WMA Pro decoder
  (libavcodec), Copyright the FFmpeg developers, https://ffmpeg.org. It builds
  the separate program skate-xma.exe and is licensed under the GNU Lesser
  General Public License 2.1 or later (rust/skate-xma/COPYING.LGPL), not
  Apache-2.0.

RAGE formats (Unlicense)
  rage-formats, rpf-archive-rs, rage-cli and rage-render, by VIRUXE, released
  into the public domain. https://github.com/VIRUXE

Rust crates
  Each crate linked into a shipped binary keeps its own license; release
  packages list them with their license texts in THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt
  (tools/third-party-notices.py).

Enhanced compatibility port
  Maintained by Stonqz27, 2026.
  Based on becaring/SK8V 1.1.8 at commit 9fbef449b51178521495d3f9dd90c91f98f7fe18.
